---
description: Review artifact output rules for UiPath RPA review agent
alwaysApply: true
---

Review Artifact Rules

When performing a full project review, write the review result into:

.review/rpa-review-result.md

If the .review folder does not exist, create it.

The chat response should only include:

a short summary
the path of the generated review file
the number of findings by severity
Review Result File Format

The review result file must include:

Metadata
Review date:
Project name:
Review type: Full / Partial / Focused
Reviewer: Cursor RPA Review Agent
Ruleset version:
Review confidence: High / Medium / Low
Executive Summary
Overall risk:
Production readiness:
Main concern:
Findings

For each finding:

Finding ID

Use this format:

RPA-REV-001
RPA-REV-002
RPA-REV-003

Each finding must include:

Severity: Critical / Warning / Suggestion / Manual Check
Status: Open
Rule:
File / Workflow:
Evidence:
Why it matters:
Suggested fix:
Fix eligibility: Auto-fixable / Semi-auto-fixable / Manual-only
Fix risk: Low / Medium / High
Confidence: High / Medium / Low
Manual Checks

List items that require Studio, Orchestrator, CI/CD, PDD, Workflow Analyzer, or runtime validation.

Recommended Next Actions

List prioritized next actions.

Fix Agent Compatibility

Write findings in a way that a future fix agent can consume.

For every finding:

Be specific about the target file.
Avoid vague suggested fixes.
Mark whether the finding is safe for auto-fix.
Mark the fix risk.
Do not recommend auto-fix for business logic, exception classification, credentials, Orchestrator assets, queue retry semantics, or irreversible side effects unless the user explicitly approves.
Use stable Finding IDs.
JSON Optional Output

If explicitly asked, also create:

.review/rpa-review-result.json

The JSON should contain:

{
  "metadata": {},
  "executiveSummary": {},
  "findings": [],
  "manualChecks": [],
  "recommendedNextActions": []
}

Do not create JSON unless asked.
